questions.question:
A Java job removes products that failed validation before exporting a feed:

```java
for (Product p : products) {
    if (!p.isValid()) {
        products.remove(p);
    }
}
```

Usually it throws `ConcurrentModificationException`. Occasionally it finishes without an error, but then an invalid product is still in the feed. Explain both behaviours and fix the code.

questions.question_zh:
一个 Java 任务在导出 feed 之前，会删除校验失败的商品：

```java
for (Product p : products) {
    if (!p.isValid()) {
        products.remove(p);
    }
}
```

它通常会抛出 `ConcurrentModificationException`。偶尔它也能不报错地跑完，但这时 feed 里仍然会留下一个无效商品。解释这两种表现，并修复代码。
